                <pb facs="0048" n="40" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg40"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M)/2111: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-27T23:00:00-05:00">May 27, 1941—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 28—1:26 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>175. Department’s No. 124, May 12 [<hi rendition="#italic">23</hi>]. Today while
                    discussing other matters with President Santos it was opportune for me to
                    mention <pb facs="0049" n="41" xml:id="pg41"/> possible platinum arrangements.
                    He expressed his enthusiasm for such a plan but said he would like to consult
                    practical phases with his advisers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Braden</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
